# ============================================================================
# .blacklist — Exclude files and folders from the Second Brain MCP server
# ============================================================================
#
# One pattern per line. Lines starting with # are comments.
# Patterns are case-insensitive. Changes take effect within 30 seconds.
#
# ── FOLDERS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# End with \ or / to mark as a folder. Matches the folder and all contents.
#
#   .\copilot          Relative folder in vault root (.\ prefix optional)
#   copilot            Same as above — bare names are treated as root folders
#   .\.obsidian        Dot-folder in vault root
#   Resources\Temp     Nested folder
#   Test\              Trailing backslash marks it as a folder
#
# ── FILES ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# End with a file extension (e.g., .md, .txt, .tmp). Matches by filename.
#
#   !Folder_Embeddings.md   Exact filename match (in any folder)
#   Untitled.md             Any file named Untitled.md
#   Thumbs.db               System file
#
# ── WILDCARDS (*) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The * wildcard matches any characters, including path separators.
#
#   *secret*           Any file or folder with "secret" anywhere in the path
#   *.tmp              Any .tmp file
#   temp_*.md          Any .md file starting with "temp_"
#   Resources/*/old    "old" folder at any depth under Resources (matches all contents)
#   *backup*           Any path containing "backup"
#
# ── ABSOLUTE PATHS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Full absolute paths can also be specified. Works for paths both inside
# and outside the vault root.
#
#   C:\Users\John\Documents\#Obsidian#\John\Test   Folder inside vault (same as .\Test)
#   C:\Users\John\Documents\Archive                Folder outside vault
#   C:\Users\John\old-notes\file.md                File outside vault
#
# Absolute paths inside the vault are equivalent to their relative counterparts
# but can be useful when generating blacklist entries from scripts or logs.
#
# ============================================================================
# Examples — remove the # to activate
# ============================================================================

# --- Folders ---
#.\copilot
#.\.obsidian
#.\.ClineData
#.\.trash
#Test\
#Resources\Temp

# --- Files ---
#!Folder_Embeddings.md
#Thumbs.db
#.DS_Store

# --- Wildcards ---
#*.tmp
#*secret*
#temp_*.md
#*backup*
